  "_notes": "Shinjitai (新字体) -> kyūjitai (旧字体) mapping derived from the 1949 Tōyō and post-1981 Jōyō simplifications. Keys are single shinjitai code points; values are lists of candidate kyūjitai forms. A one-element list is an unambiguous rewrite. A multi-element list flags a shinjitai whose correct kyūjitai depends on meaning (e.g. 弁 → 辨/瓣/辯/辮: 弁護士=辯, 弁当=辨, 花弁=瓣, 弁髪=辮; 画 → 畫/劃: 絵画=畫, 区画=劃). The downstream caller emits '[A|B|C]' for multi-entry positions and asks the LLM to resolve by context. For shinjitai with a valid bare-classical sense identical to the shinjitai (余 'I', 缶 'jar', 芸 'rue'), only the modern simplification target is listed; the classical sense is rare in modern subtitles and is accepted as a known limitation. Characters whose shinjitai equals their kyūjitai are deliberately absent — the converter leaves unmapped characters verbatim. The table is curated and intentionally extensible: a regression test in tests/test_japanese.py pins the well-attested common entries so future edits cannot silently drop them; new entries can be added by appending to this object.",
